course: dictionary
lesson: 8790
title: Shanghai, a city and a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shanghai is a proper noun, which means it is the name of one special place, so it starts with a capital letter. «Every Sunday Mei-Lin in London video calls her cousin in Shanghai» tells you Shanghai is a place in another country, far from London.
explain: Shanghai is a huge city on the east coast of China, and one of the biggest cities in the world. «Shanghai is 8 hours ahead of London in winter, so a London morning is a Shanghai evening.» The word ahead is the clue: the clocks there show a later time.
explain: Shanghai can also be a verb, but it is old and informal. «I got shanghaied into tidying the classroom» does not mean you went to China. Swap in «tricked into» and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
fact: Shanghai is a city, so it is a proper noun and always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Shanghai is a huge city on the east coast of China, and one of the biggest cities in the world.
fact: A megacity has more than 10 million people, and Shanghai is one of the megacities.
fact: The Chinese name for Shanghai means roughly «on the sea».
fact: As a verb, «shanghai» is old and informal. It means to trick or force someone into doing something they did not want to do.
exercise: In «Shanghai is 8 hours ahead of London in winter», what kind of word is Shanghai? | A verb, meaning to travel | An adjective, describing a colour | *A proper noun, the name of a city
exercise: «I got shanghaied into tidying the classroom.» What does shanghaied mean here? | *Tricked into doing something you did not want to do | Painted with bright colours | Sent home early | Given a prize for tidying
exercise: Mei-Lin video calls her cousin in Shanghai. In which country is Shanghai? | *China | Egypt | Japan | Australia
test: A megacity has more than how many people? | Over 500 children | *Over 10 million people | Over 100 people
test: «Shanghai is 8 hours ahead of London in winter.» If it is 9 am in London, what time is it in Shanghai? | *5 pm | 8 am | 9 pm | 1 am
exam: Which sentence uses shanghai as a verb? | *I got shanghaied into helping with the sports day | Shanghai is a huge city on the east coast of China | Mei-Lin calls her cousin in Shanghai every Sunday
